From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Luke Craig <lacraig3@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 14:31:58 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] target/i386: deliver INT 0x80 from user mode without the BQL

cpu_handle_exception() holds the BQL around every do_interrupt unless the
target's TCGCPUOps.exception_bql_free says otherwise.  x86's SYSCALL and
SYSENTER are helpers that take no lock, but INT 0x80 (the i386 system
call, also usable from 64-bit tasks) is a software interrupt raised as an
exception, so a guest's INT 0x80 system calls serialize on the BQL under
MTTCG: a getppid/close storm through INT 0x80 runs at the same rate at
-smp 2 and -smp 4.

Implement exception_bql_free for x86: true for vector 0x80 raised by an
INT instruction at CPL 3 in protected mode, outside SVM guest mode and
SMM.  Delivery reads the IDT, GDT/LDT and TSS, pushes the frame, loads
CS/SS and the hflags and clears IF/TF/VM/RF/NT: the vCPU's own state and
guest memory.  The engine's system-call entry and the syscall trap run
their consumers on the vCPU thread, as they do from the SYSCALL and
SYSENTER sites.  Faults during delivery leave through
raise_exception_err() as from any helper (a triple fault's reset request
included), and a task gate runs switch_tss(), as a far CALL or JMP through
one does from a helper.  Nothing touches the local APIC; interrupt
acceptance stays in x86_cpu_exec_interrupt() under the BQL.  The storm
then runs 2.2 times faster at -smp 4.

Every other exception and vector, real mode, SVM guest mode and SMM keep
the BQL.

SPDX-License-Identifier: LGPL-2.1-or-later
Origin: new
---
 target/i386/tcg/helper-tcg.h        |  3 +++
 target/i386/tcg/system/seg_helper.c | 33 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 target/i386/tcg/tcg-cpu.c           |  1 +
 3 files changed, 37 insertions(+)

diff --git a/target/i386/tcg/helper-tcg.h b/target/i386/tcg/helper-tcg.h
index b3c8240eba4359be042ed2f581a75f55c5c6cf15..fc330af7f359620b5ef4edd94a9eb235fe563111 100644
--- a/target/i386/tcg/helper-tcg.h
+++ b/target/i386/tcg/helper-tcg.h
@@ -37,6 +37,9 @@
  */
 void x86_cpu_do_interrupt(CPUState *cpu);
 #ifndef CONFIG_USER_ONLY
+bool x86_cpu_exception_bql_free(CPUState *cpu);
+#endif
+#ifndef CONFIG_USER_ONLY
 bool x86_cpu_exec_halt(CPUState *cpu);
 bool x86_need_replay_interrupt(int interrupt_request);
 bool x86_cpu_exec_interrupt(CPUState *cpu, int int_req);
diff --git a/target/i386/tcg/system/seg_helper.c b/target/i386/tcg/system/seg_helper.c
index 106490d23a7b84d54babbc575d9cc7ffa8d9ffad..1e7a515b0b9b06536ca25b5b0a0ac80cd74b5115 100644
--- a/target/i386/tcg/system/seg_helper.c
+++ b/target/i386/tcg/system/seg_helper.c
@@ -150,6 +150,39 @@ void handle_even_inj(CPUX86State *env, int intno, int is_int,
     }
 }
 
+/*
+ * May x86_cpu_do_interrupt() deliver cs->exception_index without the BQL?
+ *
+ * Yes for INT 0x80 executed at CPL 3 in protected mode (the i386 Linux
+ * system call, also used by 32- and 64-bit tasks on x86_64 kernels), outside
+ * SVM guest mode and SMM.  Delivery reads the IDT, GDT/LDT and TSS through
+ * the softmmu TLB, pushes the frame on the kernel stack, loads CS/SS (hflags)
+ * and clears IF/TF/VM/RF/NT: the vCPU's own state and guest memory, which
+ * the memory core locks for itself where it must (MMIO).  The engine's
+ * system-call entry (panda_sc_enter_c) and the syscall trap (x86_sc_i386)
+ * run their consumers on the vCPU thread, as they do from the SYSCALL and
+ * SYSENTER sites, which take no lock.  A fault while delivering (#GP, #NP,
+ * #PF, #DF) leaves through raise_exception_err() as it would from any
+ * helper; a triple fault calls qemu_system_reset_request(), which helpers
+ * already call without the BQL.
+ * A task gate in the IDT runs switch_tss(), the code a far CALL or JMP
+ * through a task gate runs from a helper without the BQL.  Nothing here
+ * touches the local APIC: interrupt acceptance stays in
+ * x86_cpu_exec_interrupt(), under the BQL.
+ *
+ * Every other exception and vector, real mode, SVM guest mode (event
+ * injection and the VMCB) and SMM keep the BQL.
+ */
+bool x86_cpu_exception_bql_free(CPUState *cs)
+{
+    CPUX86State *env = cpu_env(cs);
+
+    return cs->exception_index == 0x80 && env->exception_is_int &&
+           (env->cr[0] & CR0_PE_MASK) &&
+           (env->hflags & HF_CPL_MASK) == 3 &&
+           !(env->hflags & (HF_GUEST_MASK | HF_SMM_MASK));
+}
+
 void x86_cpu_do_interrupt(CPUState *cs)
 {
     X86CPU *cpu = X86_CPU(cs);
diff --git a/target/i386/tcg/tcg-cpu.c b/target/i386/tcg/tcg-cpu.c
index e8ed088466f9778d0b9ef37afee2dc1d5d4415d3..64f425da495c4c98614a6095bbc1b758263350f9 100644
--- a/target/i386/tcg/tcg-cpu.c
+++ b/target/i386/tcg/tcg-cpu.c
@@ -226,6 +226,7 @@ const TCGCPUOps x86_tcg_ops = {
     .tlb_fill = x86_cpu_tlb_fill,
     .pointer_wrap = x86_pointer_wrap,
     .do_interrupt = x86_cpu_do_interrupt,
+    .exception_bql_free = x86_cpu_exception_bql_free,
     .cpu_exec_halt = x86_cpu_exec_halt,
     .cpu_exec_interrupt = x86_cpu_exec_interrupt,
     .cpu_exec_reset = x86_cpu_exec_reset,
